WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.200
-Our next guest has her comedy
special "The Hustler"

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.767
premiering March 9th on YouTube.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:08.334
Please welcome the very funny
Kelsey Cook.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.200
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:16.033
♪♪

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:19.267
-Wow, hi, thank you so much.

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:21.033
It's great to be here.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:24.033
I am from Spokane, Washington,
originally,

00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:26.601
and I've been on tour a lot
the past year.

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:29.467
And sometimes people go,
"You ever get scared to perform

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:31.634
in dangerous places
like New York City?"

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:35.767
I'm like, "Spokane is the meth
capital of America."

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.868
Okay? I am the danger.

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:40.567
Spokane is rough.

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:43.968
Last time I was home, I got an
Uber driver named Bones.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:45.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.167
And he looked like a Bones.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:50.067
I cancelled the ride
immediately, of course.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.133
I'm not going to get into a car
with my ex.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:58.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.267
What a crazy name.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:03.901
Bones must get 200 ride
cancellations an hour.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:06.968
I don't even think
he owns a car.

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:11.434
I think he just sits in bed and
collects a $5 cancellation fee.

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:14.501
[ Laughter ]
Every 30 seconds.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:17.000
He's probably a millionaire.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.501
I need to make a driving profile
with a fake photo

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:21.033
and say my name is Stabs.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.834
I'd like a new laptop.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.934
I'm in a new relationship,

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:29.367
and we had that conversation
about labels

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:31.667
because I felt ready to be
called boyfriend and girlfriend.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:34.467
And he goes, "You know, being in
my 40s, I feel like

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.868
I'm a little old to be called
somebody's boyfriend.

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.734
But if you call me
your man friend,

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.767
that sounds like I've committed
sex crimes."

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.534
So I was like, "Alright, well,
what are you going to call me?"

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:50.033
And he goes, "I'll just be like,
'This is my lady.'"

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:51.234
I was like,
"Well, that feels like

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:52.701
we're at a renaissance fair."

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:55.234
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:57.701
And I can't use the equivalent
of that.

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:01.767
I can't be like, "Mom, Dad,
I'd like you to meet my lord."

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:02.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.501
Ugh.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:09.234
And he's also a comedian.

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:12.167
And I wasn't much of a jealous
girlfriend in my 20s.

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:14.901
And then some switch flipped
in my 30s.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.400
And now when I see somebody hit
on the person I'm with,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.000
I just feel myself animorph into
the cast of "Jersey Shore."

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.234
I am ready to brawl.

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:25.467
And he does get hit on.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:28.033
When he walks on stage,
women whistle at him.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:30.400
And at comedy clubs, there's
usually a security guard

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.667
in the back to kick people out
in case they heckle.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.501
So at his shows, I've just
started to stand

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:36.634
next to the security guard.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:39.501
And if I see a woman laughing
too hard at one of his jokes,

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:40.868
I just walk up and I'm like,

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:42.601
"Hey, I'm going to have to ask
you to leave."

00:02:42.601 --> 00:02:45.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.634
"He's my favorite comedian."

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:48.434
Well, he's my lord, so beat it.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.667
Scoot.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:57.567
The last time I did "The Tonight
Show," I mentioned that

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:59.968
my entire family and I are
actually

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:02.133
world champion foosball players.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, thank you.

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:08.934
But what's fun for me,
since nobody suspects that

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:11.901
I'm a pro foosball player,
I love to hustle people.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:14.234
Right? And I usually play
against other comedians

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:15.868
on my foosball web series.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:19.267
But we did this special episode
where I went undercover in Vegas

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:22.000
and hustled drunk dudes
on the Vegas Strip.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:24.868
So, I wore this low-cut top.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:26.834
I talked in the worst voice.

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:29.267
And my camera crew and I would
go up to groups of guys.

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:32.367
And I'd go, [High-pitched voice]
"Hi, my name is Kelsey

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:34.634
and I have this web series
where I do things

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:36.934
that I've never done before
for the first time."

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:40.968
"It's called 'Pop My Cherry.'"

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:43.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:47.334
"Silly. So, I've never played
foosball before.

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:48.667
And we just found this table

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.167
and I was just wondering if you
guys wanted to play me."

00:03:53.501 --> 00:03:56.734
[ Normal voice ]
Every group of guys was like,
"Hell yeah, lady, let's go.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:58.801
Mm-hmm.
Yeah, I'll play you right now."

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:02.434
And so I would play the first
game terribly on purpose.

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:04.667
I would giggle a bunch,
spin the rods a lot.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:06.267
Really build up
their confidence.

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:09.467
And then I'd go, "Okay, so, I
think I have the hang of it now.

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:12.534
And this is Vegas, so we should
play for money."

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:15.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:19.634
And every guy would put their
whole wallet on the table.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:21.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:25.133
They'd hand me the ball and go,
"Here, you can serve first."

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:29.067
And that's when I pull out
my foosball grip glove.

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:38.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:44.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:45.734
I've never done cocaine,

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:47.634
but I would assume
it's a similar rush.

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:50.467
Alright, thank you,
I'm Kelsey Cook.

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:51.934
Thanks for having me.

00:04:51.934 --> 00:04:54.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:57.133
-Come on! Thank you so much.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:05:00.067
That's how you do it.
Kelsey Cook.

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:04.434
"The Hustler" will be available
March 9th on YouTube.

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:06.801
We'll be right back, everybody.
Come on back.

